  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="907a2fba-a735-5150-a6cf-d95085521f09" activityNameId="8315aa80-6737-5ca0-b1af-7a9a19914f15" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Sour gas, burned in gas turbine, production, MJ</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Sour gas, burned in gas turbine, production, MJ
Burning of sour gas in a turbine for on-site electricity production.;
UUID: 913d3e72-055f-3432-ab4c-18b54044fa85
Providing of compression energy by the exploitation of (sour) gas fields. 
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Data is based on the Norwegian data (offshore combined production). No information about technology. As the data is an average over all gas turbines, motors and boilers in the Norwegian gas and oil production it can be assumed that different technologies are represented.
Time period: Average of 1999-2000 is used for CH4, CO2, NMVOC, NO2 (data from the Norwegian offshore combined production). Data for CO, N2O, SO2, Hg, Radon-222 and waste heat are based on data from 1991 in Frischknecht et al. 1996, Tab. V.6.7.
Production volume: 2.98 E9 Sm3 burnt natural gas
Sampling: Data is based on the annual reports on emissions and discharges submitted by each individual operator. The emissions and discharges are estimated according to guidelines given by the Norwegian authorities and OLF (Norwegian Oil Industry Association) 
Extrapolations: Norwegian data can be extrapolated for global exploitation turbines
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_913d3e72-055f-3432-ab4c-18b54044fa85.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
